 "rationale": "Round 3 coefficients match sigma*exp(i(b K + c Jx)), K = Jy+Jz, with b and c equal to theta*n from the reported hop. CH4+: b = 0.13062 and c = -0.00434, fitted 0.13060 and -0.00434. CD4+: b = 0.13144 and c = +0.00067, fitted 0.13144 and +0.00066, after mapping the reported axis into the well 1->2 frame with the overall sign flip noted in round 1. A, B and C already equal 6 times the stabilizer-averaged tensor, for example 6*6.69826 = 40.190. I therefore replace the free series with the exponential itself, reducing 11 terms to 7. sigma is the full series in L = b0 K + c0 Jx through order 8 at the CH4+ values, with a K-only tail for orders 9 and 10; the omitted order-11 term is about 6e-6 cm-1 at most at N+=8. The isotopologue difference and the rounding of the reported axis are carried by three derivative terms. db is dE/db, taken at the midpoint b = 0.13103 so the CD4+ second-order b error cancels. dc is dE/dc, taken at b = 0.13144 so the CD4+ b-c cross term is included by telescoping. The form i(Jx E + E Jx)/2 is exactly proportional to the true derivative because [K,[K,Jx]] = 2Jx closes the rotation. dcc is the second order in c, about -sigma*dc^2/2 (about -7e-5 for CD4+), needed because CD4+ lies 0.005 from the base c; it should fit near 0 for CH4+. The likely cause of the round 3 residuals is the truncated tilt series plus the missing c^2 term: the fit-residual ratio of 250 lies between sigma*c (93) and sigma*c^2 (610), though this is inferred from scaling. Expected fits are db and dc of about 1e-3 for CH4+, and db about 4.5e-3 and dc about 0.0275 for CD4+. By hand, the reflection y<->z sends L to -L, Jx to -Jx and K to -K, and swaps wells 1 and 2, so each truncated series maps to its Hermitian conjugate and is time-reversal even. No bare scalar is added to an operator, to avoid any ambiguity in how the compiler treats it. This spec has not been compiled or fitted. The main risks are compile time for the eighth-power products of L, and the assumption that the target contains exactly this hop exponential with no further hop or centrifugal terms.",
